import ../../../testing/driver.dl

to [poll the initial viewport] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    require condition (view's window != (0 as a pointer)) reporting "Polling preceded surface creation"
    set view's width to 320
    set view's height to 500
    set view's pixel scale to 2.0

document responsive fixture:
    paragraph "Mobile first" using no UI appearance
set instance to an instance of responsive fixture
set driver to the value at (the test UI driver)
set driver's poll to (the function named "poll the initial viewport $") as a pointer
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 1280 by 900 using font "regular" with (the address of driver)
require condition ((view's width = 320) and (view's height = 500)) reporting "Initial layout retained the requested desktop viewport"
require condition ((view's layout's bounds' width = 320.0) and (view's clip's width = 320.0)) reporting "The first layout and clip disagree with the host surface"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "The first UI layout uses the actual host viewport and pixel scale."
